  "title": "Packaging: add missing build dependency on git for debian",
  "description": "Without `git` building the debian package fails as `make-version.py` is calling `git`.\n\n```\nmake  -f CMakeFiles/vcs_version.dir/build.make CMakeFiles/vcs_version.dir/build\nmake[2]: Entering directory '/wireshark/obj-x86_64-linux-gnu'\n/usr/bin/python3 /wireshark/tools/make-version.py /wireshark\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/wireshark/tools/make-version.py\", line 533, in <module>\n    main()\n    ~~~~^^\n  File \"/wireshark/tools/make-version.py\", line 516, in main\n    repo_data.update(read_repo_info(src_dir, args.tagged_version_extra, args.untagged_version_extra))\n                     ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/wireshark/tools/make-version.py\", line 455, in read_repo_info\n    repo_data = read_git_repo(src_dir, tagged_version_extra, untagged_version_extra)\n  File \"/wireshark/tools/make-version.py\", line 361, in read_git_repo\n    git_commondir = subprocess.check_output(git_get_commondir_cmd, universal_newlines=True).strip()\n                    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/usr/lib/python3.13/subprocess.py\", line 472, in check_output\n    return run(*popenargs, stdout=PIPE, timeout=timeout, check=True,\n           ~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n               **kwargs).stdout\n               ^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/usr/lib/python3.13/subprocess.py\", line 554, in run\n    with Popen(*popenargs, **kwargs) as process:\n         ~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/usr/lib/python3.13/subprocess.py\", line 1039, in __init__\n    self._execute_child(args, executable, preexec_fn, close_fds,\n    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n                        pass_fds, cwd, env,\n                        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n    ...<5 lines>...\n                        gid, gids, uid, umask,\n                        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n                        start_new_session, process_group)\n                        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/usr/lib/python3.13/subprocess.py\", line 1972, in _execute_child\n    raise child_exception_type(errno_num, err_msg, err_filename)\nFileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'git'\nmake[2]: *** [CMakeFiles/vcs_version.dir/build.make:73: CMakeFiles/vcs_version] Error 1\n```\n\nThis fixes the git check in the script to correctly check if git is installed.",
