  "discussions_data": [
    {
      "id": "80c848d49ff197232793bcc87a93431d7c67a395",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 3064155775,
          "type": null,
          "body": "The `make-version.py` script tries to guard against this:\n\n```python\ndef read_git_repo(src_dir, tagged_version_extra, untagged_version_extra):\n    # Reads metadata from the git repo for generating the version string\n    # Returns the data in a dict\n\n    IS_GIT_INSTALLED = shutil.which('git') != ''\n    if not IS_GIT_INSTALLED:\n        print(\"Git unavailable. Git revision will be missing from version string.\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return {}\n```\n\nHowever this doesn't work as `shutil.which` returns None instead of an empty string:\n\n```python\n>>> import shutil\n>>> x = shutil.which('git')\n>>> print(x)\nNone\n>>> shutil.which('git') != ''\nTrue\n>>> shutil.which('git') != None\nFalse\n```\n\nSee also https://docs.python.org/3/library/shutil.html#shutil.which",
          "author": {
            "id": 5884947,
            "username": "dveeden",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Daniël van Eeden",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/00c536bb5304097eb409787c4a770e820db2a200d04130b8ca03cbcda0f526f7?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/dveeden"
          },
          "created_at": "2026-02-06T12:03:29.939Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-02-06T12:03:29.939Z",
